+<p><strong>Pass:</strong> one real customer pays the certified partner, and the partner pays the introduction fee. One target supplies payroll, certificate, job-level margin and customer-retention evidence. It has two independently staying DIAs, one qualifying as technical final responsible. The seller-role bridge must still fund founder labour, debt, tax, capex and the conditional earn-out without breaching the reserve. <strong>Kill:</strong> no paid inspection after five qualified projects; no target has two staying DIAs; the only technical signatory leaves; normalised cash misses debt service; certificate continuity is not confirmed; or reader risk exceeds €50,000. The experiment runs beside the job. Closing does not.</p>
 </section>
 
 <div class="verdict-box">
 <h2>Verdict</h2>
 <p class="verdict"><strong>ACQUIRE, DO NOT BUILD</strong></p>
-<p>The standing obligation, employed-DIA rule and physical report make this a real operating business, but they do not grant the reader a personal route. Buy only a team and customer book that already work without the seller. The single assumption that would most change the verdict is that an affordable target exists with two independently staying DIAs and at least €150,000 of pre-normalisation EBITDA. If the search finds only owner-DIA practices or strategic-buyer prices, do not enter.</p>
