 <section class="changed">
 <h2>What changed</h2>
-<p>The obligation is standing, not new. Article 7.9 of the Besluit bouwwerken leefomgeving requires the party doing or commissioning demolition to hold an asbestos-inventory report for the affected part when asbestos is known or suspected. Buildings from before 1994 create that presumption. Post-1 January 1994 buildings and specified exceptions fall outside the general rule. The report must reach the contractor before removal. <!-- CHECK: 06-bbl-duty --></p>
+<p>The obligation is standing, not new. Article 7.9 of the Besluit bouwwerken leefomgeving requires the party doing or commissioning demolition to hold an asbestos-inventory report for the affected part when asbestos is known or suspected. Buildings from before 1994 create that presumption. Post-1 January 1994 buildings and the linked non-certified-company or private-removal cases can be excepted. The customer must give the contractor a copy before asbestos removal. <!-- CHECK: 06-bbl-duty --></p>
 <p>This separates obligation from purchase event. Owning an old building creates no automatic annual inspection budget. A renovation, maintenance opening or demolition project activates the queue. The project owner or coordinator commissions the inventory; the inventory findings and report then enter the national asbestos tracking system. <!-- CHECK: 06-lavs-flow --> Enforcement can make the file necessary, but the project's timing and procurement route decide who gets paid.</p>
 <p>The latest process-scheme amendment was published on 26 August 2026 and took effect the next day. It updated the reference to the 2025 version of NEN 2990. The official explanation says the change was limited and added no administrative burden. <!-- CHECK: 06-scheme-change --> There is no fresh regulatory wave to sell. The business must win on response time, trusted reports and repeat property work.</p>
 <p>The existing control is substantial. The certificate-holder must report changes of directors, management, owners and ultimate beneficiaries immediately to its certification body. A process certificate lasts at most three years and the certification body reviews every branch at least annually, including a sample of files. <!-- CHECK: 06-change-control --> A share purchase can preserve the legal entity, but it does not make change of control invisible.</p>
 <p>Ascert's live register showed 155 certified asbestos-inventory firms and 798 valid DIA certificates when checked. Personal DIA certificates generally last three years. <!-- CHECK: 06-register-counts --> Those are supply counts, not evidence of a shortage or of sellers. They also average several DIA certificates per firm only arithmetically; the distribution and employment status are not public.</p>
-<p>Buyer behaviour exists but is narrow. HMP says it structurally works with self-employed DIAs and offers regular assignments around Eindhoven, Arnhem and Nijmegen inside its certified organisation. <!-- CHECK: 06-hmp-demand --> This proves that a certified bureau can buy variable inspection capacity. It does not prove that a stranger can acquire the bureau, retain its employed DIA or win the same work.</p>
-<p>The pitch's kill fact is therefore only partly tested. The scheme confirms that losing the employed DIA is operationally fatal until another qualifying employee is in place. The public record cannot show whether a particular target's DIA will stay, on what package, or whether customers will follow a non-DIA owner. <!-- CHECK: 06-retention-boundary --> Those facts require a named target, employment documents and direct conversations.</p>
+<p>There is direct end-buyer behaviour, not just a rule. Stedin's 2024 EU award notice covers asbestos inventories for utility connections. It records four selected suppliers, a 17 July selection and 16 August contract date. <!-- CHECK: 06-end-buyer-award --> That is a named buyer and completed procurement. It does not show that a two-DIA bureau can qualify for the framework or establish ordinary property-manager prices.</p>
+<p>Labour demand is separate. HMP says it structurally works with self-employed DIAs and offers regular assignments around Eindhoven, Arnhem and Nijmegen inside its certified organisation. <!-- CHECK: 06-hmp-demand --> This proves that one certified bureau seeks variable inspection capacity, not end-customer demand or acquisition feasibility.</p>
+<p>The pitch's kill fact is therefore only partly tested. Loss of the last employed DIA threatens the scheme's employment condition. Loss of the sole qualifying technical final responsible person stops final signatures. Losing another DIA is capacity loss unless that person also holds one of those roles. <!-- CHECK: 06-employed-dia --> The public record cannot settle retention packages, customer continuity or certificate treatment after this exact transaction. <!-- CHECK: 06-retention-boundary --> Those facts require written certification guidance, target documents and direct conversations.</p>
 </section>
 
 <section class="whyyou">
 <h2>Why you</h2>
-<p>Capital and process discipline do the work here. The reader can map every report from quote, building history and site scope through sample identity, laboratory result, risk class, exception, signature and archive. The scheme requires a quality system, controlled documents, internal review, training records and long report retention. <!-- CHECK: 06-quality-system --> That is familiar systems work applied to a physical service, not an excuse to build an app.</p>
+<p>Capital and process discipline do the work here. The reader can map every report from quote, building history and site scope through sample identity, laboratory result, risk class, exception, signature and archive. The scheme requires a quality system, controlled documents, internal review, procurement controls, replacement arrangements and long report retention. <!-- CHECK: 06-quality-system --> That is familiar systems work applied to a physical service, not an excuse to build an app.</p>
 <p>Polish and Russian can help with CEE-owned contractors, farms, logistics buildings and property operators. English helps with institutional owners. Those languages do not replace the Dutch customer layer. Residents, municipal staff, contractors and certification auditors can all need precise Dutch. A misunderstood access limit or excluded room is not a cosmetic translation error.</p>
-<p>The personal Dutch gate is a fail. ProXia requires a DIA candidate to command Dutch in speech and writing; the examination includes theory, report and practical components. <!-- CHECK: 06-dutch-exam --> At A2, the reader does not inspect or sign. The business gate passes only through retained people: an employed DIA, a qualifying DIA as technical final responsible person, and a Dutch account owner. Put all three names and deputies in the investment memo. If one person fills all three roles, fail the target.</p>
+<p>The personal Dutch gate is a fail. ProXia requires a DIA candidate to command Dutch in speech and writing; the examination includes theory, report and practical components. <!-- CHECK: 06-dutch-exam --> Treat A2 as a fail unless the exam provider confirms eligibility and the reader obtains the DIA certificate. <!-- CHECK: 06-a2-gate --> Until then, the reader does not inspect or sign. The business gate passes only through retained people: an employed DIA, a qualifying DIA as technical final responsible person, and a Dutch account owner. Put all three names and deputies in the investment memo. If one person fills all three roles, fail the target.</p>
 <p>The precedent is Advies Lieren's acquisition of Buro Pear on 17 August 2026. The announcement says Buro Pear's seller initially kept daily leadership of ongoing projects, staff work remained unchanged, and the work would later transfer to Advies Lieren's principals. <!-- CHECK: 06-precedent-sale --> Ascert independently listed both Advies Lieren and Buro Pear with valid inventory certificates after the announced date. <!-- CHECK: 06-precedent-trace --></p>
 <p>That precedent is unusually useful because it argues against a lazy version of the thesis. Advies Lieren was already a certified operator with its own capacity. It could absorb work and transfer leadership gradually. The record proves that the deal shape exists. It does not prove that an A2 financial buyer without a qualified bench can copy it.</p>
 <p>The constraint that breaks the fit is the day job. The ninety-day search can run beside employment; ownership cannot. Customer calls, staff safety, audit findings and site exceptions do not wait for evenings. This is step two: resign only at a signed, financed closing, and only after the qualified employees sign retention agreements.</p>
