+<p>Every unreceipted number in that table is a design hurdle. Replace the €15,000 reserve with the target's payroll, debtor, tax and laboratory cycle before bidding. Any lender fee outside the stated 1.5%, personal guarantee exposure or mandatory cash top-up counts against the €50,000 ceiling.</p>
+<p>Brookz's broad construction-and-installation guidance gives an indicative 4.3–5.5 EBITDA multiple. <!-- CHECK: 06-multiple --> Its visible asbest page showed two much larger active businesses and one sold inventory bureau at €850,000 revenue and 6–10 staff. <!-- CHECK: 06-sale-pool --> The record did not show an affordable two-DIA firm, a completed price or verified profit. Apply the multiple only to like-for-like normalised EBITDA. Even if a higher value results, cap seller consideration at €275,000 to preserve the non-price cash.</p>
+<p>No earn-out is paid in year one. From year two, a tranche becomes eligible only if named employees stay and retained-customer gross profit meets the agreed test. Payment also requires post-tax, post-capex cash above the €15,000 reserve hurdle. Otherwise it defers or expires under the agreed formula. Tax, capex and earn-out are company uses; the documents must prohibit another reader cash injection. If lender or seller rejects that boundary, do not close.</p>
