-<p>The obligation is standing, not new. Article 7.9 of the Besluit bouwwerken leefomgeving requires the party doing or commissioning demolition to hold an asbestos-inventory report for the affected part when asbestos is known or suspected. Buildings from before 1994 create that presumption. Post-1 January 1994 buildings and specified exceptions fall outside the general rule. The report must reach the contractor before removal. <!-- CHECK: 06-bbl-duty --></p>
+<p>The obligation is standing, not new. Article 7.9 of the Besluit bouwwerken leefomgeving requires the party doing or commissioning demolition to hold an asbestos-inventory report for the affected part when asbestos is known or suspected. Buildings from before 1994 create that presumption. Post-1 January 1994 buildings and the linked non-certified-company or private-removal cases can be excepted. The customer must give the contractor a copy before asbestos removal. <!-- CHECK: 06-bbl-duty --></p>
 <p>This separates obligation from purchase event. Owning an old building creates no automatic annual inspection budget. A renovation, maintenance opening or demolition project activates the queue. The project owner or coordinator commissions the inventory; the inventory findings and report then enter the national asbestos tracking system. <!-- CHECK: 06-lavs-flow --> Enforcement can make the file necessary, but the project's timing and procurement route decide who gets paid.</p>
 <p>The latest process-scheme amendment was published on 26 August 2026 and took effect the next day. It updated the reference to the 2025 version of NEN 2990. The official explanation says the change was limited and added no administrative burden. <!-- CHECK: 06-scheme-change --> There is no fresh regulatory wave to sell. The business must win on response time, trusted reports and repeat property work.</p>
 <p>The existing control is substantial. The certificate-holder must report changes of directors, management, owners and ultimate beneficiaries immediately to its certification body. A process certificate lasts at most three years and the certification body reviews every branch at least annually, including a sample of files. <!-- CHECK: 06-change-control --> A share purchase can preserve the legal entity, but it does not make change of control invisible.</p>
 <p>Ascert's live register showed 155 certified asbestos-inventory firms and 798 valid DIA certificates when checked. Personal DIA certificates generally last three years. <!-- CHECK: 06-register-counts --> Those are supply counts, not evidence of a shortage or of sellers. They also average several DIA certificates per firm only arithmetically; the distribution and employment status are not public.</p>
