 <main class="wrap">
 <p class="kicker">Essay 6 of 6 · Certified inspection microfirm · from pitch 9</p>
 <h1>The certificate is not the asset. The second qualified employee is.</h1>
-<p class="lede">Before an older Dutch building is renovated or demolished, somebody may need to inspect it for asbestos and put a qualified name on the report. <!-- CHECK: 06-bbl-duty --> The apparent business is durable: buy a small certified bureau, keep the inspector, and own the customer book. The dangerous word is <em>keep</em>. A2 Dutch cannot replace the inspector, the technical signatory or the customer lead. One departure can stop production. This essay narrows the pitch to asbestos inventory and asks whether a two-inspector firm can pay both people, acquisition debt and an owner who has left a developer's salary.</p>
+<p class="lede">Before an older Dutch building is renovated or demolished, somebody may need to inspect it for asbestos and put a qualified name on the report. <!-- CHECK: 06-bbl-duty --> The apparent business is durable: buy a small certified bureau, keep both inspectors, and own the customer book. The dangerous word is <em>keep</em>. Losing the last employed DIA threatens certification. Losing the sole qualified technical lead stops signatures. Any departure cuts capacity. This essay asks whether a two-inspector firm can pay both people, acquisition debt and an owner who has left a developer's salary.</p>
 
 <section class="proposition">
 <h2>The proposition</h2>
-<p>The target is a Dutch asbestos-inventory bureau, not an asbestos-removal contractor and not a general inspection holding company. It has two employed DIA certificate-holders, a Dutch planner or account owner, a valid company process certificate and several repeat B2B accounts. The buyer takes the shares, the team, the quality system, the work history and the trading name.</p>
+<p>The target is a Dutch asbestos-inventory bureau, not an asbestos-removal contractor and not a general inspection holding company. It has two employed DIA certificate-holders, a Dutch planner or account owner, a valid company process certificate and several repeat B2B accounts. The proposed share purchase transfers the entity, team, quality system, work history and trading name. It closes only after the certification body confirms in writing how the transfer and planned personnel changes affect certificate validity. The public scheme does not settle that transaction-specific consequence. <!-- CHECK: 06-retention-boundary --></p>
 <p>The end customer is usually a property, maintenance or project manager. The purchase event is a planned renovation, maintenance opening or demolition involving a pre-1994 building. The immediate deliverable is a scoped site investigation, laboratory-backed source record and signed asbestos-inventory report. The regulated company must employ at least one DIA; the scheme also requires a DIA to perform the inventory. <!-- CHECK: 06-employed-dia --></p>
 <p>The technical final responsible person is more than a decorative certificate-holder. That person must be a DIA, must meet an experience or annual-work test, must know the quality system and signs the final report. <!-- CHECK: 06-tev-signature --> The business therefore sells field judgement plus a controlled file. Scheduling, pre-research and report assembly can improve. Sampling, exceptions and the signature remain human.</p>
 <p>The first substitute is another certified local bureau. The second is a larger environmental consultancy that can add soil, chromium-6, occupational hygiene or project supervision. The third is the customer's preferred demolition contractor arranging a separate inventory firm. The new owner does not sell removal, laboratory analysis, legal advice or a certificate in their own name. It never becomes software with a login.</p>
