+<p>Labour demand is separate. HMP says it structurally works with self-employed DIAs and offers regular assignments around Eindhoven, Arnhem and Nijmegen inside its certified organisation. <!-- CHECK: 06-hmp-demand --> This proves that one certified bureau seeks variable inspection capacity, not end-customer demand or acquisition feasibility.</p>
+<p>The pitch's kill fact is therefore only partly tested. Loss of the last employed DIA threatens the scheme's employment condition. Loss of the sole qualifying technical final responsible person stops final signatures. Losing another DIA is capacity loss unless that person also holds one of those roles. <!-- CHECK: 06-employed-dia --> The public record cannot settle retention packages, customer continuity or certificate treatment after this exact transaction. <!-- CHECK: 06-retention-boundary --> Those facts require written certification guidance, target documents and direct conversations.</p>
