 <section class="competition">
 <h2>The incumbent gets a turn</h2>
 <p>The strongest competitor is another certified acquirer. Advies Lieren's purchase of Buro Pear shows the response: combine specialist knowledge and customers, keep project leadership during transition, then move work onto an existing qualified bench. <!-- CHECK: 06-precedent-sale --> Such a buyer can pay for synergies that the reader does not have.</p>
-<p>Broader firms compete differently. Tritium markets asbestos work inside a team spanning soil, environment and sustainability, and its DIA vacancy describes projects from buildings to whole housing districts. <!-- CHECK: 06-dia-salary --> A property manager may prefer one supplier across hazardous materials and environmental work. A demolition contractor can repeatedly introduce its established independent inventory bureau without owning it.</p>
