chapters/06-certified-inspection-microfirm.html:101:<p>The <strong>€275,000 purchase-price hurdle</strong> is lower than the total funding package. Qredits currently publishes €50,000–€250,000 MKB credit, 9.95% annual interest, 1.5% one-off cost, an average five-year term and acquisition as an allowed use. <!-- CHECK: 06-qredits-terms --> A €200,000 five-year annuity at that rate is about €50,900 yearly. The 1.5% fee is €3,000. Both calculations are arithmetic, not approval or quotes.</p>
chapters/06-certified-inspection-microfirm.html:115:<p>Brookz's broad construction-and-installation guidance gives an indicative 4.3–5.5 EBITDA multiple. <!-- CHECK: 06-multiple --> Its visible asbest page showed two much larger active businesses and one sold inventory bureau at €850,000 revenue and 6–10 staff. <!-- CHECK: 06-sale-pool --> The record did not show an affordable two-DIA firm, a completed price or verified profit. Apply the multiple only to like-for-like normalised EBITDA. Even if a higher value results, cap seller consideration at €275,000 to preserve the non-price cash.</p>
chapters/06-certified-inspection-microfirm.html:124:<p>Scale is constrained by the scheme. An inventory owner cannot also own a removal company. Owning two inventory companies is generally barred unless the concern meets high DIA and report-volume thresholds. <!-- CHECK: 06-ownership-limits --> This is not a casual roll-up. Expand one certified entity, or add services that preserve independence.</p>
chapters/06-certified-inspection-microfirm.html:125:<p>Audit load also steps up with delivery. The current table requires four annual project-site assessments for one or two DIAs and fewer than 500 reports. It rises to six for three to five DIAs or 500–1,100 reports. The higher applicable criterion controls, and each tier includes announced and unannounced assessments. <!-- CHECK: 06-audit-load --> Growth buys more scrutiny, not merely utilisation.</p>
chapters/06-certified-inspection-microfirm.html:131:<p>The strongest competitor is another certified acquirer. Advies Lieren's purchase of Buro Pear shows the response: combine specialist knowledge and customers, keep project leadership during transition, then move work onto an existing qualified bench. <!-- CHECK: 06-precedent-sale --> Such a buyer can pay for synergies that the reader does not have.</p>
